<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f5f1e9">
    <meta name="description" content="Kinship is an app in development for understanding Instagram follower and following relationships from an official export you choose. Your export is processed locally, with gaps made clear.">
    <title>Kinship — A clearer picture of your connections</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/styles/site.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <div class="site-shell">
      <header class="site-header">
        <a class="wordmark" href="#top" aria-label="Kinship, back to top">
          <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span>
          <span>kinship<span class="wordmark-period">.</span></span>
        </a>
        <span class="header-status"><span class="status-light" aria-hidden="true"></span> In development</span>
      </header>

      <main id="main">
        <section class="hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line" aria-hidden="true"></span> A little more clarity</p>
            <h1 id="hero-title">Your connections,<br><em>in context.</em></h1>
            <p class="hero-lede">Followers and following tell different stories. Kinship helps you make sense of both, using an official Instagram export you choose.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
              <a class="button" href="#how-it-works">Explore how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
              <span class="quiet-note">No account connection needed</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="art-label art-label-top"><span class="tiny-cross">✳</span> A clearer view</div>
            <div class="orbit orbit-outer"></div>
            <div class="orbit orbit-inner"></div>
            <div class="orbit-fill"></div>
            <div class="orbit-center"><span class="orbit-center-mark">k<span>.</span></span><span>your view</span></div>
            <div class="orbit-node node-one"></div>
            <div class="orbit-node node-two"></div>
            <div class="orbit-node node-three"></div>
            <div class="orbit-node node-four"></div>
            <div class="orbit-node node-five"></div>
            <div class="orbit-node node-six"></div>
            <div class="orbit-tag tag-followers"><span class="tag-dot"></span> followers</div>
            <div class="orbit-tag tag-following"><span class="tag-dot"></span> following</div>
            <div class="art-label art-label-bottom">The full picture has room for unknowns <span>↗</span></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="intro-band" aria-label="The Kinship approach">
          <span class="band-symbol" aria-hidden="true">✳</span>
          <p>Not another guess about what happened. <strong>A way to see what your export actually shows.</strong></p>
          <span class="band-index" aria-hidden="true">01 / 03</span>
        </section>

        <section class="process section-wrap" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="process-title">
          <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow">The idea</p>
            <h2 id="process-title">Start with what<br><em>you know.</em></h2>
            <p>Kinship is being built around a simple principle: useful answers should not come at the cost of honest ones.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="steps">
            <article class="step">
              <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Choose your export</h3>
                <p>Use an official Instagram export you select. No Instagram login, password, or account connection.</p>
              </div>
              <span class="step-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </article>
            <article class="step">
              <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
              <div>
                <h3>See the relationships</h3>
                <p>Explore followers, following, and where the two overlap. Export contents are processed locally in the app.</p>
              </div>
              <span class="step-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </article>
            <article class="step">
              <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Keep the context</h3>
                <p>Partial or missing data stays marked as unknown. An export cannot tell you why a relationship changed or its exact timing.</p>
              </div>
              <span class="step-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="principle" aria-labelledby="principle-title">
          <div class="principle-inner section-wrap">
            <div class="principle-symbol" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
            <div class="principle-copy">
              <p class="eyebrow">Made for the grey areas</p>
              <h2 id="principle-title">Unknown is not<br><em>the same as no.</em></h2>
              <p>When an export is incomplete, Kinship does not treat missing entries as proof someone is absent. Even complete snapshots cannot prove a block, deletion, rename, or the exact date a follow changed.</p>
            </div>
            <span class="principle-index" aria-hidden="true">KNOW WHAT YOU KNOW / 02</span>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="closing section-wrap" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
          <div class="closing-marker" aria-hidden="true">✳</div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Coming into focus</p>
            <h2 id="closing-title">A more thoughtful way<br>to <em>look closer.</em></h2>
            <p>Kinship is in development. There is nothing to download yet — just a clearer way to think about the connections behind the numbers.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </main>

      <footer class="site-footer">
        <span class="footer-brand">kinship<span>.</span></span>
        <p>Independent project. Not affiliated with Instagram or Meta.</p>
        <a href="#top">Back to top ↑</a>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
